Done in "[PATCH v2 0/3] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's
mail hub" [1]:

- Patch 1 is the spec correction from v1's first patch with the Sieve
  parts removed. Dovecot answers OK to a reader's STORE and EXPUNGE
  and changes nothing, so the rights section and acceptance step 7
  now say so. Without it a correct build fails step 7.
- Patch 2 is the implementation with no Sieve. LMTP delivers each
  post to INBOX, and README.org says a post waits there until you
  move it into lists. mbsync does not sync INBOX, so a post reaches
  Fastmail and the other readers only after you move it.
- Patch 3 adds Sieve on top: lists.sieve, the Pigeonhole package, the
  dovecot.conf lines, and the spec text. Its diff is the whole
  difference.

The tree after patch 3 is identical to v1's, so the testing from v1
still holds for it. I could not test patch 2 on its own because
Dovecot is no longer installed here. Its config only drops the Sieve
plugin, which leaves Dovecot's default delivery to INBOX.

Patch 2 leaves the spec unchanged, so for now it still says Dovecot
files posts into lists. If you take patch 2 without patch 3, I will
change that line to say INBOX.

